12. Predict the Output – Queue ADT Concept
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
#define SIZE 5
int queue[SIZE];
int front = 0, rear = -1;
void enqueue(int x) {
queue[++rear] = x;
}

int dequeue() {
return queue[front++];
}
int main() {
enqueue(10);
enqueue(20);
enqueue(30);
printf(&quot;%d &quot;, dequeue());
printf(&quot;%d &quot;, dequeue());
return 0;
}
Question: Predict the output and identify the principle followed by the ADT.
Queue ADT
Operations:
enqueue(10);
enqueue(20);
enqueue(30);
Queue:
Front → 10 20 30 ← Rear
First dequeue() removes 10.
Second dequeue() removes 20.
Output:
10 20
Principle: FIFO — First In, First Out
The element inserted first is removed first.
